From ceec63e57407fbeedcf2136cdd7be67934ddc69a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasiliy Kovalev <kovalev@altlinux.org>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 07:59:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pkg/cover: temporarily mute module size mismatch log in
 canonicalizer

Suppressed the misleading `log.Errorf` that triggers when a dynamically loaded
module's coresize in the guest VM instance differs from its canonical size
parsed from the ELF file on the host.

*** THE PROBLEM ***
When fuzzing a real production kernel configuration (such as ALT Linux
JeOS/SP) with CONFIG_MODULES=y, syz-manager floods the logs with:

[ERROR] kernel build has changed; instance module intel_rapl_common differs from canonical

While this error does not abort the syz-manager startup, it litters the log
output and flags the module as `discard = true`, blinding the fuzzer to the
module's coverage (KCOV).

*** TECHNICAL ANALYSIS & PROOF ***
Investigation shows that the modules on the host and inside the VM are
binary identical, sharing the exact same Build ID:

  Host ELF Build ID:
  Build ID: defa1647b9ba769dc813d17ebded659b28a37bac

  Guest VM sysfs Build ID:
  # xxd /sys/module/intel_rapl_common/notes/.note.gnu.build-id
  00000010: defa 1647 b9ba 769d c813 d17e bded 659b

However, their sizes strictly mismatch:
  Host `size` utility output (raw sections):
  text    data     bss     dec     hex filename
  79262   31180     704  111146   1b22a intel_rapl_common.ko

  Guest `coresize` (allocated layout in memory):
  # cat /sys/module/intel_rapl_common/coresize
  122880

This 11,734-byte discrepancy occurs because the Linux kernel loader
allocates module memory by grouping sections (.text, .data, .rodata)
by page protection attributes and aligning each region to the page boundary
(4096 bytes on x86_64). The guest reports `coresize` as aligned memory blocks
(122,880 / 4096 = 30 pages exactly) plus runtime kernel overhead, while
syzkaller calculates the size based on the raw vmlinux/ELF layout.

*** IMPACT & WORKAROUND ***
Since forcing CONFIG_MODULES=n (Built-in) is not acceptable when testing
downstream production kernels, muting this log keeps the syz-manager output
clean.
---
 pkg/cover/canonicalizer.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/cover/canonicalizer.go b/pkg/cover/canonicalizer.go
index 6edb3db..a4ebbfb 100644
--- a/pkg/cover/canonicalizer.go
+++ b/pkg/cover/canonicalizer.go
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ func (can *Canonicalizer) NewInstance(modules []*vminfo.KernelModule) *Canonical
 		canonicalAddr := uint64(0)
 		canonicalModule, found := can.modules[module.Name]
 		if !found || canonicalModule.Size != module.Size {
-			log.Errorf("kernel build has changed; instance module %v differs from canonical", module.Name)
+			// log.Errorf("kernel build has changed; instance module %v differs from canonical", module.Name)
 			discard = true
 		}
 		if found {
-- 
2.50.1

